     1,
     "Dear lavaan users, I have a few questions regarding the recent <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.06112\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.06112&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792412712330000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3VXiJnytWlHAuSoppGQvCq\">arXiv paper</a> on SEM modeling with composites in lavaan.<div><br></div><div><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">In the Supplementary Material, under the &quot;Variances&quot; output, the composite variables (Quality, Performance, CorpSocResp, Attractiveness) do not have standard errors, and the lavaan output does not put a period in front of the construct names, which seems to indicate that these are &quot;total&quot; variances not residual variances. See below for screenshot. </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"><u>My questions are:</u></span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"></span></p><ol start=\"1\" type=\"1\" style=\"margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in\"><li style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">How are these variance parameters calculated for the composite variables </span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">(Quality, Performance, CorpSocResp, Attractiveness)?</span></li><li style=\"margin-bottom:0in;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Are these specified as causal-formative or composite-formative?</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"></span></font></li></ol><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.75in;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">A.<span style=\"font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">    </span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">If the former, why is there no estimated residual variance?</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"></span></font></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.75in;line-height:normal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">B.<span style=\"font-size:7pt;line-height:normal;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;;font-size-adjust:none;font-kerning:auto;font-variant-alternates:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-numeric:normal;font-variant-east-asian:normal;font-feature-settings:normal\">     </span></span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">If the latter, why are these values non-zero</span><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"> (given that residual variances in composite models are typically fixed to zero)?</span></font></p><p style=\"margin:0in 0in 0in 0.75in;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"><b><br></b></span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Any guidance or insight would be greatly appreciated. </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Many thanks,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0in;line-height:normal;font-size:medium;font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"font-size:10.5pt;font-family:Roboto\">Janine</span></p></div><div><div><br></div></div><div><b>Supplementary Material Output Screenshot: </b></div><div><img alt=\"Variance_Output.jpg\" width=\"368px\" height=\"534px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/lavaan/attach/405202279fb67/Variance_Output.jpg?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>Citation</b>: <span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Schamberger, T., Schuberth, F., Henseler, J., &amp; Rosseel, Y. (2025). Structural Equation Modeling with Latent Variables and Composites. </span><i style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">arXiv preprint arXiv:2508.06112</i><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">.</span></div>"
